ses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-7.$ Therefore, $x=-7$ is a *simple* root."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d48e2a0-1a76-5eec-a98c-4a7eb16f70cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Multiplicity of a Root Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565858} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ea4cfe-3c2b-531a-b7fa-3167daa6ad38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is a simple root of even multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565934} {:answer/id #uuid "bf72962b-ac8f-5b9c-8f14-e9632a0c6017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is not a root of $p(x)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565985} {:answer/id #uuid "c8681ab5-0854-580f-a01d-5117b98125ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is a simple root" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566001} {:answer/id #uuid "ce1f700e-ca83-50c0-a87a-7c914e000acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is a multiple root of even multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73918c51-a1f9-582d-9ee3-270673767b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=2$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565858} :answer-field/id #uuid "599c8793-e8c3-5306-b56b-04269b939632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13c802b0-f24f-5ef6-be2f-44ec40da3fdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-141143" :question/problem "![](images/67/67c87009cbafcf40172b4de6cae4cb57e37660dd15235f67500c2a0532d42dee.png)\n\nA part of the graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements is true?" :question/worked-solution "| Multiplicity | Sketch | Sketch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ \n\n (Simple Root) | ![](images/5a/5a0221f93c65a1eeb4503604a558a6da81c4c7af81c2c52cc35ecf3d189fe99f.png) | ![](images/d5/d556b4edf39181eebb7ec87c344d6f657a6875ecd2745405eaf5351ccaff6f96.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Even | ![](images/9d/9d14c2588da2ee9c9f5bbc32a70791146bed609ea0d6d5912aeaa2edab02e2d7.png) | ![](images/28/28ad9248a9a509e3a44937d0438fb2366f550a22360d01b9b6a29bcac41357e8.png) |\n| $>1$ \n\n (Multiple Root) \n\n Odd | ![](images/3a/3ae81378cb3c918dd5b7730519eb5a91e949f88eef9f03f4910f4ab8fb3cd5a9.png) | ![](images/95/9506a7ce4031f1f6244c0110c3235f66ea5652bb53548a032732869cf21f5997.png) |\n\nIt's possible to determine information regarding the multiplicities of the roots of a polynomial from its graph.\n\n- If the graph intersects the $x$-axis but is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *simple* root $x=a.$\n\n- If the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ we have a *multiple* root $x=a.$ Furthermore:\n\n- If the graph touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *even*.\n\n- If the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=a,$ the multiplicity of a root $x=a$ is *odd*.\n\nIn our case, the graph is *tangent* to the $x$-axis at $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ is a *multiple* root. \n\nFurthermore, the graph crosses the $x$-axis at $x=2.$ So, $x=2$ has *odd* multiplicity.\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is a multiple root of odd multiplicity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565681} {:answer/id #uuid "077eb7e5-61fe-5718-b55a-2b30f9c2f3a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{3}{4}x(x-1)(x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565689} {:answer/id #uuid "5760f119-2844-592e-b4bc-1ffb9056581a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2x(x-1)^{2}(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565821} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a8460d-b922-5d90-a177-f59cb8734c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-8{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565993} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9d9f52-14d2-5d50-9588-0460d9c70c08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{7}{3}{x}^{2}(x-1)(x-2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03a72d79-34ff-583b-9f8b-56a973a8ea21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565681} :answer-field/id #uuid "92540022-5b3a-549e-bcbf-092250f5beb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e919c69-a07f-59d0-9a4f-80f07bde8e75" :question/math-academy-id "q-38674" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b22cee7a07af8745945c07bebf63fac213e26dd210b2e41762784fed64a1532.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=0,$ $x=1,$ and $x=2.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=0,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=1,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=2,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=-5{x}^{2}(x-1)^{2}(x-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c3d270-4f2a-53d7-8062-8d2e9cbcdce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438278} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8eef91-6406-5add-96a7-f9eabef0d91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f8eef91-6406-5add-96a7-f9eabef0d91c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438279} :answer-field/id #uuid "1da65ceb-5594-5e44-bb39-79c87b94bf6f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739a4d76-6103-5d84-90a1-9822e2f320c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438280} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea74f05-534d-5d4b-9392-375d31647dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea74f05-534d-5d4b-9392-375d31647dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438281} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a0193f-d631-5929-9c6e-41674a92b0c3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4175bc45-7a87-5063-b600-76a60ad7f40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438282} {:answer/id #uuid "f897869b-bbb9-53aa-9454-68a151292859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4175bc45-7a87-5063-b600-76a60ad7f40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438282} :answer-field/id #uuid "92c5a7e5-4803-5105-b804-5b0e1a2d5217" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbe22a70-053f-5354-8d7b-dc32dacb2db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-38770" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd19717bd41b787346a96394ce3bc4e38fe690340bb73bd3d11139d41ff977e2.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=2$ is a simple root.\n\n- **II.** $x=-1$ is a root of even multiplicity.\n\n- **III.** $p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=2$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=-1$  has an even multiplicity because at $x=-1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement III is false. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "377d2e81-b433-5192-b5f2-5e1f0c06f2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565768} {:answer/id #uuid "56626858-9917-5e86-a480-5880f6bda1c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565817} {:answer/id #uuid "af6f95ab-c708-5e53-9fff-dc760663af8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565955} {:answer/id #uuid "d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566020} {:answer/id #uuid "e37d7018-5d40-5dcd-9b09-15c860e95b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d37635de-5c8a-521b-bbfe-c96b155ed7f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566020} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c25fadf-bd40-53ef-b6e5-84027da47699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "571594cb-dae3-572c-bed1-7b71f8315ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70812" :question/problem "![](images/75/75b9d9a0500f526670c59b4f92c28f4da8d979e39c615ae4f25ec960a80ca1e0.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n\nII. $x=0$ is a simple root.\n\nIII. $p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because at $x=0$ the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The root $x=0$ is not a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at that point, and the curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $+\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves up in the positive direction towards $+\\infty .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b68fad9-861a-5a5d-b8d5-ff1e2fa15ab7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{7}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346430} {:answer/id #uuid "8724b35c-787a-52ef-80ff-eaf99f6a667a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{5}(x-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346523} {:answer/id #uuid "94213796-5be7-57ae-81b2-17ed395cf18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346645} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ec07fb-d5b8-585e-82ea-e6c5d87d6e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}(x+2)^{5}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346910} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c1df98-76d9-50de-b003-8111fdce77bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{2}(x+2)(x-1)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94213796-5be7-57ae-81b2-17ed395cf18a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346645} :answer-field/id #uuid "db472ae2-2f21-533d-93c0-3a75b3b10cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0154a31e-007f-558f-af24-913ca9813ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-80352" :question/problem "![](images/19/1956e8c684cc03538877d3ec5d1e72d3d3f48b63341f7739b9a18962b080f1e3.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-2,x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=-2,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-2,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=0,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=1,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=1,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348372 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129147 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of a Factored Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "210c0cb2-912c-5a88-8fab-d2b221d3d8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345648} {:answer/id #uuid "578811c3-d760-5438-8269-7b591fd2e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346098} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0b1d0e-a7ac-564a-b02a-f66d4dbce1e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346127} {:answer/id #uuid "c18eb786-715d-592f-812e-faf140c5760a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347023} {:answer/id #uuid "d01fbc8b-3abd-597b-9580-d7486138bd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "578811c3-d760-5438-8269-7b591fd2e0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346098} :answer-field/id #uuid "87542a89-0c5a-559e-b96f-503f1f855e5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2fc14fca-8eab-53a0-95ef-067136b19692" :question/math-academy-id "q-80353" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b2f70dda865622ace25db16dfa55c50c746a88ec4bbc34c8560dd0f342a02ac.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=-1$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,2$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{II}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{II}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{II}.$"}]}
